& [ExistingAuthority] is already bounded in kind but not fully quantified
  + the base specification calls FieldElement content a bounded visible semantic payload
  + the base specification permits an isolated reversible P0 and typed faults
  + the provider request already limits generated tokens and forbids retry

& [ObservedGap] is numeric resource ambiguity
  + field element count is bounded but subject purpose content identifiers provenance and the field file have no byte ceilings
  + report input has no file-size ceiling
  + provider calls originally had no connection deadline total deadline or response-byte ceiling
  + a non-success provider response body could originally be copied verbatim into a fault string

& [Risk] is operational rather than semantic
  + an oversized local input or malformed loopback provider can consume disproportionate memory time context or evidence space
  + raw failure bodies can carry arbitrary provider text into durable evidence
  + resource exhaustion and disclosure do not create semantic authority but can prevent faithful execution

& [RequiredDisposition] is a closed P0 budget
  + quantify UTF-8 byte limits for host-controlled text identities field files report files and provider responses
  + impose one connection timeout and one total request timeout with no retry
  + preserve non-success response status byte count and content digest without preserving the body
  + expose budgets through the contract command and test each rejection boundary
  + retain every historical request compiler and report meaning unchanged
  - never: infer truth safety production readiness remote network authority or generalized denial-of-service resistance
